<languages />
<translate>
<!--T:1-->
On this page, we build a basic [[mw:en:"Hello, World!" program|Hello World]] page with {{SITENAME}}.

<!--T:2-->
{{SITENAME}} builds a static website from a directory of wikitext. There are three ways to install it: the standalone [[<tvar name="1">Special:MyLanguage/Installation#binary</tvar>|binary]] (Linux only), the [[<tvar name="2">Special:MyLanguage/Installation#Docker</tvar>|Docker image]] (any platform), or [[<tvar name="3">Special:MyLanguage/Installation#build-from-source</tvar>|built from source]]. This guide uses the binary or Docker, so pick whichever you have.
</translate>

----

<translate>
<!--T:4-->
Create a source directory and add a wikitext file. Any file ending in <code>.wikitext</code> becomes a wiki article. Name your entry page <code>index</code> so it builds to <code>index.html</code>, the file a browser opens at the site root.
</translate>

<syntaxhighlight lang="shell" copy>
mkdir src
echo 'Hello, World!' > src/index.wikitext
</syntaxhighlight>

<translate>
<!--T:5-->
Then build the site. The rendered pages are written to <code>dist/</code>. Pick the tab for how you run {{SITENAME}}:
</translate>

<tabber>
|-|Binary=
<translate>
<!--T:6-->
Run it in the directory that holds <code>src/</code>:
</translate>
<syntaxhighlight lang="shell" copy>
wikven build
</syntaxhighlight>
|-|Docker=
<translate>
<!--T:7-->
Mount the source and output directories into the container:
</translate>
<syntaxhighlight lang="shell" copy>
docker run --rm \
  -v "$(pwd)/src:/workspace/src" \
  -v "$(pwd)/dist:/workspace/dist" \
  ghcr.io/chaotic-ground/wikven
</syntaxhighlight>
<translate>
<!--T:8-->
The untagged image is the newest released version. To hold a build still, pin the version tag <code>:<tvar name="1">{{WIKVENVERSION}}</tvar></code> or the digest (<code>ghcr.io/chaotic-ground/wikven@sha256:...</code>); shorter tags for the major and the minor version are published too, and move as that line gains releases. A dated <code>nightly-YYYY-MM-DD</code> tag is the main branch as it stood that day, for trying a change before it is released.
</translate>
</tabber>

<translate>
<!--T:9-->
Preview the site locally, then open <code>http://localhost:8080</code>:
</translate>

<tabber>
|-|Binary=
<syntaxhighlight lang="shell" copy>
wikven serve
</syntaxhighlight>
|-|Docker=
<syntaxhighlight lang="shell" copy>
docker run --rm -p 8080:8080 \
  -v "$(pwd)/dist:/workspace/dist" \
  ghcr.io/chaotic-ground/wikven serve
</syntaxhighlight>
</tabber>

<translate>
<!--T:10-->
Opening <code>dist/index.html</code> directly also works, though some links and assets resolve correctly only when served. To publish it online, see [[<tvar name="1">Special:MyLanguage/Deploying</tvar>|Deploying]].

<!--T:11-->
== Setting the title of the site ==

<!--T:12-->
For configuration, create a [[<tvar name="1">Special:MyLanguage/Configuration</tvar>|<code>.wikven.yaml</code> file]] in your <code>src</code> directory.
</translate>

<syntaxhighlight lang="shell" copy>
cat <<EOF > src/.wikven.yaml
config:
  Sitename: My Site
EOF
</syntaxhighlight>

<translate>
<!--T:13-->
Build again with the same command as before, and the site is titled "My Site".

<!--T:14-->
== Adding a second page ==

<!--T:15-->
Every <code>.wikitext</code> file becomes a page. Add another one and link to it from the first with <code><nowiki>[[...]]</nowiki></code>:
</translate>

<syntaxhighlight lang="shell" copy>
echo 'This is the help page.' > src/Help.wikitext
echo 'Read the [[Help]].' >> src/index.wikitext
</syntaxhighlight>

<translate>
<!--T:16-->
Build again: the home page now links to <code>Help.html</code>, and the link works with no server. See [[<tvar name="1">Special:MyLanguage/Pages</tvar>|Pages]] for how file names map to page titles and namespaces.

<!--T:17-->
== Adding a template ==

<!--T:18-->
Templates, the main reason to reach for {{SITENAME}} over Markdown, let you reuse content. Put a <code>Template:</code> page in your source and transclude it with <code><nowiki>{{...}}</nowiki></code>:
</translate>

<translate nowrap>
<!--T:20-->
<syntaxhighlight lang="shell" copy>
<tvar name="1">echo "</tvar>'''Note:'''<tvar name="2"> {{{1}}}" > "src/Template:Note.wikitext"
echo '{{Note|</tvar>Rebuild the site after every edit.<tvar name="3">}}' >> src/index.wikitext</tvar>
</syntaxhighlight>
</translate>

<translate>
<!--T:19-->
Build again: the home page now shows the note. See [[<tvar name="1">Special:MyLanguage/Pages#templates</tvar>|Pages#Templates]] for parameters and more.
</translate>

